HDDS-11860.description:
Address [review comment|https://github.com/apache/ozone/pull/6652#discussion_r1854345430] from HDDS-10821:

bq. let's have another method to handle array?  The {{GatheringByteChannel}} works more efficient in that way

{code:java}
  public static long writeFully(GatheringByteChannel ch, ByteBuffer[] buffers) throws IOException {
    long written = 0;
    for(int i = 0; i < buffers.length; i++) {
      while (buffers[i].remaining() > 0) {
        final long n = ch.write(buffers, i, buffers.length - i);
        if (n < 0) {
          throw new IllegalStateException("GatheringByteChannel.write returns " + n + " for " + ch);
        }
        written += n;
      }
    }
    return written;
  }
{code}

Also,

bq. according to the javadoc, `n == 0` is a valid case.

